title: Ch2
position: 404,-519
---
<<if $Blind == true>>
	The work was hard, but it came with its rewards. 
	<<if $dadMech == true>>
		Your help was essential in keeping the whole station running.
	<<endif>>
	These people really believed in what they were doing and so did you.
	And they might even have had a shot at creating a free Jovian system. 
	But unfortunately with the come of the successful treaty that stopped the Shatter, the Blind lose a lot of their followers. 
	That on top of the opening of the Pons and the arrival of both Venuvian and Martian military force, drove the rebellion on the ground.
<<elseif $Martian == true>>
	Apart from some minor incidents here and there the conflict never exploded into a real war. 
	<<if $dadSoldier == true>>
		Your job was mostly containing small uprising here and there in the system, but not much more. 
	<<elseif $dadMech == true>>
		Your job ended up being fixing and refurbishing old spy drones from earth into full fledged support systems for the inhabitants of the jovian system.
	<<endif>>
	But luckily those days ended when the Marsuvian alliance managed to secure a successful treaty with Earth. 
	The latter would open back up the water supplies to the jovian system, and give them partial freedom while remaining in control of europa and io's resources.
	While Martian and Venuvian would deploy troops in the system, so to avoid father endangerment on Jupiter. 
	Shortly after the Pons was opened, a neutral station shared between the three forces. 	
<<endif>>
You would have thought going back to your normal life, would have taken longer. 
But everything moved so fast after those day. And everything felt so weird for some reason.
Not having to worry about water anymore. 
Working as much as possible to rebuild to keep living.
With that lingering anger.
Of knowing all that could have been avoided
But there're also so many good memories from those years.
There were your friends always making you laugh. Sully always being there and creating troubles.
There was also her. The day you met her in Ganymede. your dinners out at the rational.
Your first apartment, that old sofa, where you grew closer. 
where you hoped you'd grow old together.
When Kher was born you two were the happiest people on the Jovian system. 
<<if $Blind == true>>
	But soon your duty towards the Blind started clashing with your family.
	That kind of life is a risky one, you couldn't keep doing both. 
<<elseif $Martian == true>>
	But soon your duty towards your comrades started clashing with your family.
	The martian asked you to take long term station for 10 years on an out of system location.
<<endif>> 
	-> Choose Duty.
		<<if $Blind == true>>
		You spend the next five years working closely with Grig. And you manage to make a difference.
		Thank to you the Blind's station turns into a proper base of operation for the group.
		But circumstances change, and priority switch.
		When you get the news of her passing you immediately decide to go back to your life, to your child.
		<<elseif $Martian == true>>
		You spend the next 5 years secretly working on surveillance drones. And you manage to make a difference.
		The money are good and you know your family is taken care of.
		But sometimes life gets in the way, circumstances change, and priority switch.
		When you get the news of her passing you immediately decide to go back to your life, to your child.
		<<endif>> 
		<<if adjust_status(0,1,0,0)>><<endif>>
	-> Choose Family.
		The following 5 years are the best of your life, just the three of you, in that old workshop.
		But sometimes life gets in the way. When she got sick you didn't know how to handle it, but you had to find a way. 
		If not for her, for your child. 
		When she passed your life turned gray again.
		<<if adjust_status(0,0,1,0)>><<endif>>
<<jump Ch3>>
===
title: Ch3
position: 641,-656
---
Time really flies. 
7 years went by in a second. 
You kept working as a mechanic, raising Kher as best as you could.
Being a single dad it's not always the easiest. 
But having your own workshop helps with that.
So much that you're even able to have enough time to bring your kid to the rational.
It took them two weeks of annoying you and interrupting you mid work to convince you 
When you go pick them up from school on ganymede to finally go there, they look at you.
Kher: Hey dad, can Kazimierz hang out with us today?
-> No kiddo, today it's just the two of us. 
	The calming sound of the ship turning on helps you ignore your kid's upset face. 
	-> so Kher how did it go today? 
		Kher: ok.
		-> Just drive silently 
		-> Listen kid I know you wanted your friend with us 
			But I really wanted to spend some time just you and me
			is that ok? 
			you smile at them. 
			Kher: I said ok. don't worry.
			<<jump rational>>
	-> Just silently drive towards the rational.
		<<jump rational>>
-> Sure I don't see why not.
	The calming sound of the ship turning on, cover your kid and their friend's chatter.
	<<declare $Hick= true >><<jump rational>>
===
title: rational
---
You arrive at the rational, the place is packed full and it took you a minute for them to find you a seat. 
<<if $Hick == true>> 
	The three of you sit in the fake leather chair, while the waitress serves you your menu. 
<<elseif true>>
	The two of you sit in the fake leather chair, while the waitress serves you your menu. 
<<endif>>
You pick up the menu and read through it.
-> pick the Barszcz 
	It doesn't take you that long to settle on the Barszcz, you always felt more focused after good plate of it.
-> pick the NutriMix 
	It doesn't take you that long to settle on the NutriMix, you always felt stronger after good shake.
-> pick the Insekczyk 
	It doesn't take you that long to settle on the Insekczyk, you can actually find people more tolerable after it.
The evening flies by in a second. 
You find yourself in the ship right outside the workshop, your kids get out of the ship, while you finish turning down all the systems.
You see them enter the place and turning on the light.
You're about to switch of the JPS when you get a message from the integrated log.
<<if $Martian== true>>
	The commander's contact pops up in your messages with a location attached.
	you wonder what job will she have for you this time.
<<elseif $Blind>>
	Grig's contact pops up in your messages with a location attached.
	you wonder what job will he have for you this time.
<<endif>>

-> Go to the location. 
	When you get back home you find the kid sleeping with their book still in their hand.
	Another day has past
	<<if adjust_status(0,0,0,1)>><<endif>>
-> Turn the system down and go back home.
	You get in the house and get to work to finish a project you've been stuck on 
	Kher decides to help you out, and so you two work together. 
	By the end of the day you tuck them into bed and you know,
	another day is over.
	<<if adjust_status(1,0,0,0)>><<endif>>
===
title: alphaDialogue
---
Everything is wet when you wake up from cryosleep. 
When you first took the spacecraft to get out of the jovian system you promised yourself you would never go back. 
But here you are, the prodigal child back in their homeland. 

Memories are weird when you wake up from cryo. 

-> why was I even here? 
	Dad: You were here for me kiddo. 
	You look around but see no one. You shook away the And then remember the message.
	It came by mail what, 6 months ago now? they wrote you about your dad's sickness. 
	Dad: Came here to say your final goodbye to your old man?
	Dad: What a lucky father I am.
	-> What's happening?
		Dad: Don't worry about it.
		Then you remember, he is being treated in Febris hospital in Ganymede. 
	-> What sickness was it again?
		Dad: I don't think it's that important now kiddo.
		Then you remember, he is being treated in Febris hospital in Ganymede. 
	-> Where was he staying.
		You frantically look through your messages. 
		Six months of spam are a lot to sift through. 
		But here it is... He is being in Febris hospital in Ganymede. 
===